# Written business idea (draft)

Working title: TableSync (name TBD)

Problem: Small restaurants like my parents' 40-seat place in San Jose run on thin margins, and their scheduling, inventory, and vendor ordering live in spreadsheets, paper, and group texts. Off-the-shelf POS suites are expensive and built for chains.

Idea: A lightweight, low-cost web tool for independent restaurants that tracks inventory against daily sales, flags low-stock items, and drafts supplier orders. Start with one restaurant (my parents') as the design partner, then expand to nearby family-run restaurants.

Why me: I grew up doing the books and inventory counts in the back office of a restaurant, and I'm a CS grad who can build it (Python, web dev, basic ML for demand forecasting). First in my family to finish a 4-year degree.

First 90 days: build an MVP for inventory + order drafts, run it at the family restaurant for 4 weeks, measure hours saved and waste reduced, then sign 3 paying pilot restaurants.

